# MadGraph5 batch script: g g > t t~ at LO (QCD).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - External octets (gluons) feeding a quark line: the f(1,2,3) triple-gluon
#     vertex resolves through the f → trace color rules, giving a genuine
#     NCOLOR=2 amplitude (CF = [[16/3,-2/3],[-2/3,16/3]], same external color
#     content as pp_to_bb_qcd2/P1_gg_bbx). Complements uux_to_uux (T·T Fierz)
#     with the f → trace half of the SM color vocabulary.
#   - Massive final state (top mass in the massive-fermion currents), so
#     sqrt(s) must clear 2*MT ~ 346 GeV.
#   - One concrete subprocess => the matrix element is matrix1 (no matrix9).
#
# MadEvent output (default): `launch` builds matrix1_optim.f for the timing
# comparison and integrates the partonic cross section. lpp=0 => fixed-energy
# partonic gluon beams, so the result is the partonic sigma-hat.
generate g g > t t~
output gg_to_ttx -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
